This folder contains code adapted from EntanglementDetection.jl by Y.C. Liu:
https://github.com/ZIB-IOL/EntanglementDetection.jl

The selected source and white-noise driver were provided through
EntanglementDetection.jl_private. The source checkout commit and SHA-256
hashes of the original files are recorded in UPSTREAM.json.

The public project's MIT copyright and permission notice is retained in
LICENSE.upstream. No license file was present in the supplied private checkout;
this notice does not relicense its additional code.

Included: eigenvalue workspaces, state approximations, LMO types and methods,
tensor conversions, Frank-Wolfe distance/callback code, separable-ball radii,
and the results/Liding/white_noise_bounds.jl driver.
Excluded: upstream datasets, saved results, examples, optional Tullio extension,
other robustness/detection drivers, and the Roots dependency.

Local changes:
- Place the selected core inside PDGR and use a relative module import.
- Set option defaults to the supplied results/Liding/both.jl configuration.
- Add option validation and cooperative time limits; return only completed
  bound updates if the time limit interrupts an oracle or witness enumeration.
- Remove the internal unconditional seed-zero reset so the configured seed
  controls each probe. Seed zero retains the original behavior.
- Omit an unused distance overload with undefined dims/bases variables.
- Extract only the separable_ball_radius functions from the certification files.
- Keep the witness for the strongest lower bound; upstream could replace it
  with a later weaker witness without lowering the reported bound.
- Reject witness budgets too small to construct the minimum local net with
  an explicit error naming the required size.
